## How we work: specs first

Changes start from a spec in [`specs/`](specs/):

- `specs/product.md`: who it's for and what it should do
- `specs/architecture.md`: how it's built
- `specs/features/NNN-name/`: one folder per feature, with `requirements.md` (testable acceptance criteria), `design.md` and `tasks.md`

For a new feature, copy an existing feature folder (or write one from scratch), take the next number, set `Status: Draft`, and get it reviewed before building. Add it to `specs/features/README.md`.

## Pull request checklist

- [ ] The relevant spec exists and is up to date (requirements, tasks ticked, status)
- [ ] Tests cover the new or changed requirements
- [ ] `make check` passes locally
- [ ] README.md / CONTRIBUTING.md updated if usage, configuration or setup changed
- [ ] No secrets, and no disabled lint/security rules without a comment saying why
